<GuideLayout 
  title="High-Compression Shapewear Trends in B2B"
  description="Analyze the booming intersection of activewear and shapewear, and learn how to source high-compression products for your collection."
  publishDate="June 26, 2026"
>
  <p>The lines between shapewear and activewear have completely dissolved. Today's consumers want the aesthetic benefits of a waist trainer with the performance and comfort of gym leggings. This 'Shape-Active' category is currently the fastest-growing sector in B2B sourcing.</p>

  <h2>The 'BBL Effect' in Activewear</h2>
  <p>Scrunch-butt designs and high-waisted compression bands are no longer niche; they are core requirements for a successful leggings line. Our R&D team has developed a '3D-Sculpt' knitting technique that provides targeted compression to the waist while lifting and contouring the glutes without restricting movement.</p>

  <h2>Fabric Density Matters</h2>
  <p>For shapewear-inspired activewear, fabric weight (GSM) is key. We typically recommend a 280-320 GSM Nylon/Spandex blend. This ensures total opacity (squat-proof) and provides the necessary 'hold' to smooth the silhouette while remaining breathable for intense workouts.</p>

</GuideLayout>
